  "description": "Let's Catch the Lion: shogi on a three by four board with four pieces a side, designed for children and solved as a win for the second player. The chick promotes to a hen, captured pieces change sides, and getting your lion to the far rank wins -- provided it survives there.",
  "summary": [
    "On a 3 by 4 board, each side has a lion (its king), a giraffe, an elephant and a chick.",
    "The giraffe steps one square straight, the elephant one square diagonally, and the chick one square forward; a chick reaching the far rank becomes a hen.",
    "A piece you capture changes sides and goes into your hand; instead of moving, you may drop it on an empty square.",
    "Win by taking the lion, or by getting your own lion to the far rank and surviving there."
  ],
